      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-11-15_WidnesExaminer_art0063" n="art0063">
        <head>UNTOUCHED MEAL.</head>
        <p>THE UNTOUCHED MEAL.</p>
        <p>People who Starve with Food on</p>
        <p>the Table.</p>
        <p>" No, I simply cannot eat." Actual tragedy is suggested by these siraplo words, so often heard fall from the lips of ex- hausted bread-winners and over-worked wive° and mothers. ,Loss of appetite: that is the genesis of the trouble that sooner or later reveals itself ng Indigestion or Nervous Dyspepsia, with Violent Headaches, Lack of Energy, Loss of Cillour, Low Spirits, Severe Backache, and other srmptows• Beware of •Loss of A_ppetite!, You. must keel). up your strength. Exhaustion, 'if long ktr tinned, is bound to produce serious menTP" nervous and muscular debility.</p>
