      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-11-15_WidnesExaminer_art0127" n="art0127">
        <head>CHOKED WITH PHLEGM.</head>
        <p>CHOKED WITH PHLEGM.</p>
        <p>A Fifeshire Man's Cough that hurt, cured by one bottle of VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CUIIE.</p>
        <p>There is danger in the cough that hurts, danger that some of the delicate -mechanism of the body may give way under the strain, and serious complications follow. That is the kind of cough from which Mr. John Methven, of New Farm Cottages, Newton of Falkland, 'Fifeshire, N. 8., suffered, but was so easily and quickly cured by Veno's Lightning Cough, Cure, though everything else had proved useless. Mr. Metliven. says: "I suffered from a bad cough and had tried innumerable so-called cures without the least benefit, the strain of coughing was really terrible, it racked my whole body, and started pains in my sides and stomach, till I was afraid to cough at all. But, of course, I had to cough, for the phlegm kept choking up the air passages and it was desperately hard to bring it up. After months of this suffering I tried Veno's Light- ning Cough Cure, and what a relief ! With the, first dose or two I -could bring up the phlegm quite easily, the cough did not trouble me a bit, and one bottle of Veno's completely cured me." Veno's Lightning Cough Cure is a safe and sure remedy for all diseases of chest, lungs, and throat, in children or adults. Price 9id., Mk, and 2/9, of all chemists.</p>
