        <head>Youths Stop a Department.</head>
        <p>Youths Stop a Department.</p>
        <p>There were last night signs of a settle° gleatiiCe a strike which has been in progress f°r,-54-0' days in the wire rope department of )Le": Rylands' works, and which led to the choir° this section of the industry. ‘,O Old The apprentices there came out bec3ll--; were asked to fill in • sheets showing theirre dividual work, and they feared this Was Jude to them being placed on piece rates. ol department was stopped through the abseil' er the boys, and the men thus thrown olltd., pressed their willingness to support the 1a4411e Mr. Field, the general manager, seen bY tbere Examiner" representative yesterday-, eatd,:p rr was a misunderstanding. The sheets Ncr't-hee quired for office checking purposes and - was no intention to introduce piece rates. Act' Mr. C. Dukes and a number of delegate!,' -Of ing for the youths, had a conference Winlit firm yesterday afternoon. The result is njifY the employers offered to considerablyr 133"011' the sheet scheme. The new scheme will 1),,e AO' mitted to a mass meeting of the strikers °were and last evening the prospects of pea° very favourable.</p>
