        <head>MAY QUEEN DEAD—cont</head>
        <p>MAY QUEEN DEAD—cont</p>
        <p>field, secretary; Mr. J. Moss, treasurer' 1 Messrs. H. Brereton and P. Fletcher. AO Stockton Heath Wesleyan Sunday School S. Choir and Church: Mr. G. Whitfield, 1,i1%. rf* Moss, Mr. G. Miller, Mr: W. Twiss, gr" fgei: Hughes (secretary Wesley Guild), 'Miss A shej; ton (class leader), Mrs. Deakin, Mrs-‘,l ~.4. Mrs. Whitfield, Mrs. T. Brereton, Mrs- -,0.0' Mrs. Cliffe, Miss Taylor, Miss Frith, Miss of and Miss Speakman. There were also present represent_atif;ii. other Bands of Hope affiliated to the Lill" The Floral Tributes. , Itandsome floral tributes were sent l-01' James Dodds, "Father, _Mother, Sisterv.oioo Brother," Warrington Band of linPn sus° (floral crown), Hill Cliffe and Stockton United Band of Hope, Stockton neath, leyan 'Choir and Yount Ladies' Class, z'afor; Heath Wesleyan Girls' Society Class, Baptist Band of Hope, Cairo-street PtIA-Or',. Hope, Mr. and Mrs. G. Whitfield, Mr. al' per' F. Grounds, Mr. and -Mrs. S. Appletnian'rs. Appleton, Mr. and Mrs. Todd, Mr. and H. Walker, Mr. T. Barnes and staD, Brooks and family, Miss Robins, Coalsie,a May Vernon, Eva Tanner, " Dollie and 11 Mrs. Taylor and Ethel, Maggie, fieggr Willie Ravenscroft, Lily Manssuer, 11',,5, Grounds, "Evelyn," and "The Neiglib°</p>
