      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-11-15_WidnesExaminer_art0310" n="art0310">
        <head>Clampitt.</head>
        <p>Clampitt.</p>
        <p>Winskill, Heyes, Ruddick, Gorry, Cheethani, Barlow and Tighe. Davidson, Scott, Bland, Barnes. Danson. 13ROUGHTQN RANGERS..</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-11-15_WidnesExaminer_art0311" n="art0311">
        <head>TO-day at Wilderspoal.</head>
        <p>TO-day at Wilderspoal.</p>
        <p>A keen and interesting game should ensue between Warrington " A " and Broughton "A," at Wilderspool. The teams will be: Warrington—J. Brown; Baker, Shaw, Dain- tith and Waywell ; Brown and Douglas; Naylor, Harmer, Tranter, Critchley, Boardman and Green.</p>
        <p>Broughton Rangers—Harris; Harrigan, Slater, J. Manley and Plested; Mundy and Butter- worth; Beetham, Roberts, Aspey, W. Manley, T. Howard, Tomkins, or Quigley.</p>
        <p>A RECRUIT FROM WALES. Warrington Secure New Half-back.</p>
        <p>Mr. Bradshaw received, a telegram on Thurs- day afternoon that Warrington had effected a smart capture in South Wales. For over a week about a dozen N.U. clubs had representatives in Abertillery seeking to capture Stan. Young, the expert young half-back of that club. -Mr. Barber went there on Thursday on behalf of the Warrington Club and secured the player, to the chagrin of the representatives of the other clubs. • • Young is described as one Of the smartest "stand off" half-backs in Welsh football,. and has learned the , game with Ab.ertillerY• His services were so valued that he was selected to play in the inter-county match between Glamor- gan and Monmouth. Mr. R. T. Gabe, the South Wales critic, writ- ing as recent as last Monday in the "Athletic News," said: "Young ran well—never across the field—before parting with the ball. . showed "a. fine conception of the reverse pass . . . and should be heard of again in repre- sentative football." The same,writer said that Young was cleverer than the average half-back. Stan. Young travelled to Warrington yester- day, and to-day will be found a place in the second team in the match at Wilderspool with Broughton Rangers "A " team. His advent ought to attract a large crowd.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-11-15_WidnesExaminer_art0312" n="art0312">
        <head>SCHOOLBOY FOOTBALLERS.</head>
