        <p>SENIOR CONSERVATIVE CLUB.</p>
        <p>Team Competition—First Round. The surprise of this week's matches was the great victory St. Austin's No. 2 gained over cal very strong team from Town Hall Ward, at, this was all the more surprising in view of tl"" fact that F. Cowap, of the losing side, won th.e first game by 52. However, George Holland, who is in great form at present, gave his tenni the lead by beating J. H. Allen 70, this being a really smart performance. The St. Austin's captain, C. Cooke, although getting well on in years, still knows how to PI billiards, as was evidenced by his win over H. Wells. With one game to play, St. Austin were leading by 45, and as W. Smellie succeecl,e_e in above holding his own with H. Collin, Pi club secretary, they entered the next round 10 virtue of a good win. Another ,of the Town Hall teams had to bite the dust in their game with Howley, who, paper, look like going far in the competition,</p>
