        <p>The solution of a probe In II The world would be a pleasanter and healthier place to live in if there were no smoky coal fires. Nevertheless we must of necessity have fires in winter, and so for years the smoke nuisance has gone on. Now the solution of the difficulty has arrived. Gas fuel makes no smoke and serves every purpose hitherto accomplished by means of coal fires. For warming houses, providing ever ready hot water, for cooking, for light, gas is the most convenient, cleanly, efficient and economical agent. Pamphlet U 136 deals more fully with this question. Can we send you a copy, or serve you in any other way? The British Commercial Gas Association, 47, Victoria Street, London, S.W.</p>
