        <p>pointed Councillors Clarke, Pearson, Bottom- ley, Mclntyre, Dukes, J. Hallows and Warbur- ton a, suh-committee to consider the cost and urgency of adopting the water carriage system throughout the whole of the township. A sub- committee to select a site for a public conveni- ence was also appointed. Both will report at an early date. Labourer Runs Amok. Philip Berry, labourer, liimberley--drive, Stockton Heath, was charged at the local Petty Sessions on Tuesday with assaulting Louis Clarke, and with doing damage to the extent of 2s. 16d. to drinking utensils, the property. of the landlord of the Hat- ton Arms.—lt appeared complainant was seated in the Hatton Arms', when Berry, without any, provocation, rushed at him and gave him a black eye and loosened his teeth.—Berry was further charged with refusipg to quit.—The Chairman, Mr. Harvey Talbot, said' the Bench considered it a most brutal assault, and Berry might have done great damage to complainant. , Accused w,ould have to pay £5, or go to prison for two months' hard labour.</p>
